---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REMOVAL_ADDRESS } from "../lib/launch.ts";
---

<Base>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">Effective date: 7 September 2026.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      The Rupee Fund is a FOSS United community initiative run by community members. The community
      team manages the launch notification list. We adopt the privacy standards in the <a
        href="https://fossunited.org/privacy-policy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-link">FOSS United privacy policy</a
      >, dated 7 February 2024, with the local rules below. These local rules define our data use
      and take precedence where the source differs. We do not adopt the source's wider uses for
      marketing, profiling, event tickets, or ownership transfers. Foundation roles named in the
      source do not become Rupee Fund roles through adoption. Later changes to the source do not
      change this policy automatically.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-2">What we collect</h2>
    <ul class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>Your name.</li>
      <li>Your email address.</li>
      <li>The time of your consent, signup, and latest update.</li>
      <li>The page that you used to join.</li>
      <li>The amount each month that you say you can give.</li>
      <li>The number of months that you say you can give, if you answer.</li>
      <li>The question that you ask the team, if you ask one.</li>
      <li>Whether you tick the box for monthly updates.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      We keep this data to send you one email when the fund opens, to send you monthly updates if
      you tick the box, and to plan the fund. Your answers about money bind you to nothing. We take
      no payment. We hold no payment details. Access to your answers is limited to the people who
      administer the list and the services that process it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-2">Storage and retention</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      Cloudflare hosts this site and stores the list. The team can export the list to prepare the
      launch email. We retain entries for launch planning and notification. We have not set a fixed
      deletion date. Removal from the mailing list retains your entry as described below.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-2">Your IP address</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      We read your IP address when you send the form. We use it to prevent abuse. When your browser
      runs JavaScript, we also send it to Cloudflare with the bot check below. We do not store it in
      your list entry. Cloudflare also processes connection data to provide hosting and abuse
      protection.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-2">Bot protection</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      When your browser runs JavaScript, the form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to tell a person apart
      from a bot. Cloudflare states what Turnstile collects in the <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-link">Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-2">Fonts</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      Each page loads fonts from <a
        href="https://fonts.google.com"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-link">Google Fonts</a
      >. Google receives your IP address.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-2">Profile photos</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      The Team page loads profile photos from GitHub. GitHub receives your IP address when your
      browser requests these photos.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-2">How to leave the list</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-8">
      Send an email to <a href={`mailto:${REMOVAL_ADDRESS}`} class="inline-link"
        >{REMOVAL_ADDRESS}</a
      >. We take you off the list. We keep your entry, and we mark it as removed, so that a later
      signup cannot add you again. Ask at any time.
    </p>

    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Back to home</a>
  </div>
</Base>
